From 82f3569a065b017c36b31e3cc6b1f4ad04e37a22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshkamdar67 <harshkamdar67@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:13:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] vulkan: the Q4_0 decode attention kernel reads the
 tagged mask, one token per workgroup

The kernel takes the mask with the keys near the query tagged, the bias table and the sinks per token, so no mask
per head is built at one or two tokens. A hidden key is skipped before its K is read, and a workgroup serves one
token: with two streams in one cache, the blocks of the other stream cost nothing. Any number of tokens up to 8.
